#grammatical sentences

# 1. the mother sleeps

h mhtera koimatai.      

# 2. the mother, that is tired, sleeps

h mhtera, poy einai koyrasmenh, koimatai.   

# 3. she, who is tired, sleeps

ayth, h opoia einai koyrasmenh, koimatai.  

# 4. the mother, who sleeps, is tired

h mhtera, h opoia koimatai, einai koyrasmenh.  

# 5. Peter petted the brown dog

o Petros xaidepse to kafe skyli.    

# 6. Peter petted the dog, who is hungry 

o Petros xaidepse to skyli, to opoio einai peinasmeno. 

# 7. the mother hugged Peter, whom she loves

h mhtera agkaliase ton Petro, ton opoio ayth agapaei.   

# 8. Peter hugged her, whom he loves

o Petros agkaliase aythn, thn opoia aytos agapaei. 

# 9. Peter, that loves animals, petted the dog.   

o Petros, poy einai filozwos, xaidepse to skyli.   

# 10. Peter, that loves animals, petted the dog, which he adopted

o Petros, poy einai filozwos, xaidepse to skyli, to opoio aytos yiothetise. 

# 11. Peter, who loves animals, petted it, that has brown fur

o Petros, o opoios einai filozwos, xaidepse ayto, poy exei kafe trixwma.  

# ungrammatical sentences

# 12. gender agreement violation between determiner and relative pronoun

h mhtera, to opoia einai koyrasmenh, koimatai.

# 13. gender agreement violation between determiner, proper noun and adjective

to Petros, o opoio einai filozwo, koimatai

# 14. case violation: object in nominative (its relative pronoun in accusative)

h mhtera agkaliase o Petros, ton opoio ayth agapaei.   

# 15. case violation: relative pronoun in nominative

o Petros agkaliase aythn, h opoia aytos agapaei. 

# 16. transitive verb without object

o Petros agkaliase.

#17. intransitive with object

h mhtera koimatai to skyli.

#18. noun and pronoun without determiner

skyli, opoio einai peinasmeno, agapaei Petro.

